digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "N11" [label="(0,0,0) Currently, conjugated polymer single-crystal thin films are difficult to manufacture despite their ideal properties for high-performance electronics."];
  "N12" [label="(6,1,0) Electronegativity differences between carbon and heteroatoms in conjugated polymers create localized molecular dipoles due to asymmetric electron distribution."];
  "N13" [label="(7,1,0) From the thermodynamic perspective, molecular dipoles may serve as subtle modulators to influence the energy landscape of π-π stackings, thus lowering the energy barrier towards a single-crystal state."];
  "N14" [label="(8,1,0) On the kinetic front, molecular dipoles are expected to accelerate nucleation by fostering highly-ordered initial states and contribute to more uniform and rapid crystal growths."];
  "N15" [label="(0,0,0) If molecular dipoles can modulate energy landscapes thermodynamically and accelerate nucleation kinetically, then they could potentially address both the thermodynamic and kinetic barriers in conjugated polymer crystallization."];
  "N16" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction: The phenomenon is difficult single-crystal thin film fabrication, and molecular dipoles could address both thermodynamic and kinetic barriers, therefore molecular dipoles may be a key factor to enable single-crystal thin film growth."];
  "N17" [label="(9,1,0) Currently, accelerated nucleation is often accompanied by high-density random crystal nuclei, leading to polycrystals with abundant grains."];
  "N18" [label="(10,1,0) Currently, molecular dipoles are highly sensitive to both molecular configurations and stacking conformations."];
  "N20" [label="(11,4,0) Currently, these external force approaches are constrained by the lack of nanoscopic controls over twisted molecular configurations."];
  "N24" [label="(0,0,0) If multiple alignment methods fail at the nanoscopic level, then achieving single-crystal growth requires a method that provides nanoscopic control over molecular configurations."];
  "N26" [label="(12,1,0) Currently, achieving a delicate equilibrium between localized molecular rotations and comprehensive chain alignments remains elusive, and complex dynamics hampers precise modulation of crystallization at the thin-film level."];
  "N31" [label="(14,1,0) The nano-CMDO strategy uses a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor where molecular dipoles rotate conjugated backbones in response to perpendicular electric field, while alkyl-modified parallel plates regulate side chains."];
  "N5" [label="(3,1,0) Single crystals with perfect coplanar conformations, minimum energetic disorders, and enhanced carrier mobility are ideal platforms to access peak semiconducting performances."];
  "N6" [label="(3,0,8) Reference knowledge: If conjugated polymers achieve better molecular structure-property relationships and improved charge transport physics, then their carrier mobilities and charge transport properties can be significantly improved."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes and evaluates a nanoconfined molecular-dipole orienting strategy, nano-CMDO, in which a spatial-electrostatic nanocapacitor applies a perpendicular electric field to orient dipole-bearing conjugated-polymer backbones while regulating side-chain alignment, aiming to drive non-epitaxial self-assembly into microscale single-crystal thin films with ultralow energetic disorder and high charge mobility.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When a polymer-crystallization strategy is mechanistically motivated, provides a concrete nanoscale-control design, and is supported by successful thin-film examples with improved disorder and mobility metrics, it warrants further development and evaluation as a promising route to high-quality conjugated-polymer single-crystal films."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Because accelerated nucleation can generate high-density random nuclei and molecular dipoles are sensitive to molecular configurations and stacking conformations, controlling dipoles is a plausible route to influence early crystallization states."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) The difficulty of conjugated-polymer single-crystal thin-film fabrication and the nano-CMDO mechanism together motivate proposing a nanoconfined molecular-dipole orienting strategy for precise assembly of conjugated polymers into single-crystal thin films."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) In the proposed nano-CMDO strategy, implementation centers on a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor that uses a perpendicular electric field and alkyl-modified parallel plates."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) A design that combines perpendicular-electric-field rotation of molecular dipoles and conjugated backbones with alkyl-plate regulation of side chains is a plausible way to coordinate localized molecular rotations and chain alignments."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Because existing external-force alignment approaches are constrained by insufficient nanoscopic control over twisted molecular configurations, achieving single-crystal growth motivates methods that provide nanoscopic control over molecular configurations."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Single-crystal conjugated-polymer platforms, with minimized energetic disorder and enhanced carrier mobility, are suitable targets for improving charge-transport and semiconducting performance."];
  "N11" -> "N16" [label="abduction-phenomenon"];
